# Budget Tracker Frontend

A responsive React-based frontend for tracking income, expenses, and due dates. This app allows users to log financial transactions, categorize them, and view upcoming payments or income based on frequency and due dates.

---

## Features

- Add, edit, and view income and expense transactions
- Filter transactions by category and due date (This Week, This Month, Next Month)
- Calculate total income, expenses, and net balance
- Supports recurring transaction frequencies (once, weekly, biweekly, monthly, annually)
- Dynamic UI with conditional rendering based on login state

---

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

Make sure you have the following installed:

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v18 or higher)
- npm (comes with Node.js)

---

### Installation

1. Clone this repository:

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/plager20/budget-tracker.git
   cd budget-tracker

   ```

2. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```

### Running the App

To start the development server:

    ```bash
    npm run dev
    ```

This will automatically open the app in your default browser using Vite

### Technologies Used

    React 19
    React Router DOM
    Vite
    ESLint

